# Seed bootstrap — {{ project_slug }}

One-shot guide after `seed new`. **Delete this file when you are done**;
`seed sync` will not recreate it (Copier keeps deleted template paths deleted
on update). Use `copier recopy` / a fresh seed if you want it back.

## 1. Trust tools and install

```bash
mise trust && mise install
uv sync --all-groups
```

## 2. Sanity check

```bash
{{ project_slug }} --help
{{ project_slug }} Alice

task               # short CI list at repo root
task test_core     # unit + coverage + lint
task test          # full gate + docs

cd ci && task      # finer CORE targets
cd docs && task    # Zensical targets
```

## 3. Fill in the project

- Extend the CLI in `src/{{ project_slug }}/cli.py` (argparse for now)
- Grow tests under `tests/`
- Edit docs under `docs/content/` (Zensical / `mkdocs.yml`)
- Set real GitHub / PyPI secrets when you enable publish workflows

## 4. Day-to-day

| Command | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `{{ project_slug }} …` | Run the console script |
| `task test_core` | Unit + coverage + lint (no docs) |
| `task test` | Full gate including docs |
| `task fix_lint` | Auto-fix isort / black / markdown |
| `task docs` | Serve docs via Zensical (`cd docs && task` for more) |
| `./scripts/release.sh patch` | Bump version, commit, tag |

## 5. Syncing the seed later

```bash
seed sync          # confirm, then apply catalog updates
seed sync -y       # non-interactive
```

Managed files follow the template; paths you deleted stay gone unless you
recopy them on purpose.
